+# Pre-Ship Review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Reviewer pass before end-of-week ship. Report only — no code changed.
+Scope: `packages/nextjs` frontend + config, plus contract registration.
+
+Severity legend: **ship-blocking** (do not ship until fixed) / **should-fix** (fix before or right after ship).
+
+---
+
+## Ship-Blocking
+
+### 1. USDC is hand-added to the auto-generated `deployedContracts.ts` — next deploy wipes it and breaks the whole page
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:50` (USDC entry) + `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts:14` (empty `{}`)
+- The header of `deployedContracts.ts` literally says "autogenerated… do not edit manually or your changes might be overwritten." USDC (`0x8335…2913`) is Circle's external token, not a contract this repo deploys. It was pasted into the generated file. The next `yarn deploy` regenerates this file and the `USDC` key disappears. Every `contractName: "USDC"` read and the `deployedContracts[8453].USDC` import in the page then fail — balance read breaks and Approve breaks.
+- **Fix:** Move the USDC `{ address, abi }` block into `externalContracts.ts`:
+  ```ts
+  const externalContracts = {
+    8453: {
+      USDC: { address: "0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913", abi: [/* … */] },
+    },
+  } as const;
+  ```
+  Then in the page import from the scaffold contract layer / hooks rather than the raw `deployedContracts` file, and revert `deployedContracts.ts` to only what the deploy generates (`Payouts`).
+
+### 2. Uses raw wagmi `useWriteContract` — resolves on signature, not on confirmation
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:6,21`
+- `isPending` from raw `useWriteContract` flips back to `false` the moment the wallet returns the tx hash — before the block confirms. Combined with issue #3/#4 below, the user can re-click while the tx is still in-flight. It also skips SE-2's tx tracking/notifications.
+- **Fix:** Use `useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" })` (and a second instance for `USDC`), which waits for block confirmation and wires up the SE-2 transactor/notifications.
+
+### 3. No four-state button flow — Approve and Send Payout render simultaneously
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+- Both buttons are always visible together. There is no allowance read, so the app can't tell whether approval is even needed, and a user can click **Send Payout** before approving (or before approval confirms) → `transferFrom` reverts. This is the exact "two buttons at once" failure the flow is meant to prevent.
+- **Fix:** Add `useScaffoldReadContract` for USDC `allowance(owner, PAYOUTS.address)`. Show exactly one primary button: if `allowance < amount` → **Approve**; else → **Send Payout**. Gate on a single amount/recipient-valid check.
+
+### 4. Approve button not locked through the full cycle (double-approve window)
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:100-106`, handlers `36-47`
+- `disabled={isPending}` only. There is no `approvalSubmitting` (click→hash gap) and no `approveCooldown` (confirm→cache-refresh gap), and no allowance refetch. User can submit duplicate approvals.
+- **Fix:** Add both states, set `approvalSubmitting` at top of handler and clear in `finally`, set `approveCooldown` after the await + `setTimeout(refetchAllowance, 4000)`, and `disabled={isPending || approvalSubmitting || approveCooldown}`.
+
+### 5. No network gate — user on wrong chain clicks Send and eats a silent error
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (entire connected branch, `72-116`)
+- The only branch is connected vs not-connected. A wallet connected to Ethereum/Arbitrum/etc. will render the live Approve/Send buttons and the write will silently fail against the wrong chain. SE-2's header `WrongNetworkDropdown` is not sufficient per the flow requirement.
+- **Fix:** Branch on `useChainId() === base.id` (or `targetNetwork.id`). On mismatch, render a `useSwitchChain`-driven **"Switch to Base"** button in the same primary-CTA slot instead of the action buttons.
+
+### 6. Wallet connect is a paragraph of text, not a button
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+- `{!isConnected ? <p>Please connect your wallet to send a payout.</p> : …}` — the canonical AI mistake. There is no Connect button on the page body.
+- **Fix:** Render `<RainbowKitCustomConnectButton />` (from `~~/components/scaffold-eth`) as the primary element when disconnected.
+
+### 7. SE-2 default branding throughout (tab title, footer, README) — trust/ship blocker
+- **Tab title:** `packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx:11-12` → `title: 'Scaffold-ETH 2 App'`, and `packages/nextjs/utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts` → `titleTemplate = "%s | Scaffold-ETH 2"`. Every tab reads "… | Scaffold-ETH 2".
+  - **Fix:** Set title to "USDC Payouts" (or product name) and change the template to `"%s | USDC Payouts"`; update the description off "Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2".
+- **Footer:** `packages/nextjs/components/Footer.tsx:50-74` → "Fork me" → `github.com/scaffold-eth/se-2`, "Built with ❤ at BuidlGuidl", and a public Telegram "Support" link.
+  - **Fix:** Replace with this project's repo/support links or remove.
+- **Header:** `packages/nextjs/components/Header.tsx:92,95` → `alt="SE2 logo"`, `src="/logo.svg"`, label "Scaffold-ETH".
+  - **Fix:** Replace logo + label with the app's brand.
+- **README:** repo root `README.md` is the stock Scaffold-ETH 2 template README.
+  - **Fix:** Replace with a README describing this Payouts dApp.
+
+### 8. Verify the deployed contract on Basescan (must confirm manually)
+- **Contract:** `Payouts` at `0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2` (from `deployedContracts.ts:10`).
+- I cannot confirm verification status from the repo. Open the address on basescan.org and confirm the green "Contract" ✅ with readable source. Unverified = trust red flag for a payments app.
+- **Fix if unverified:** `yarn verify --network base`.
+
+---
+
+## Should-Fix
+
+### 9. Hardcoded `bg-black text-white` page wrapper — breaks DaisyUI theming
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65`
+- Bypasses the theme system; the header's `SwitchTheme` toggle and `prefers-color-scheme` are ignored; light-mode users get a forced black page. Also `border-gray-700` on the feed cards (`121`) is a hardcoded color.
+- **Fix:** `bg-base-200 text-base-content`; feed cards `border border-base-300`.
+
+### 10. Recipient uses a raw `<input type="text">` instead of `<AddressInput/>`
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84`
+- No ENS resolution, no validation, no blockie/paste handling. Value is force-cast `recipient as 0x${string}` (`55`) with no address check — a malformed value goes straight into a payout tx.
+- **Fix:** `<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="0x… or ENS" />` and gate Send on a valid address.
+
+### 11. No `<Address/>` display of the Payouts contract
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (nowhere)
+- Users can't see/verify the contract they're sending USDC through. The feed also renders `from`/`to` via a hand-rolled `shorten()` (`13`, `122-124`) instead of `<Address/>`.
+- **Fix:** Show the Payouts address with `<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} />`; use `<Address/>` for the feed's from/to.
+
+### 12. No USD value next to USDC amounts
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:74-76,126`
+- Balance and payout amounts show bare "… USDC". (USDC ≈ $1, but the amount should still be presented as a dollar figure for clarity/consistency.)
+- **Fix:** Display `$` alongside amounts (USDC is 1:1) or via the balance/price helpers.
+
+### 13. Errors are swallowed to `console.error` — user sees nothing
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46,59-61`
+- Both handlers `catch (e) { console.error(e); }`. A failed approve/pay (revert, rejection, insufficient balance) gives the user no feedback.
+- **Fix:** Use `notification.error(getParsedError(e))` from `~~/utils/scaffold-eth`.
+
+### 14. DaisyUI `loading` class applied to the button itself
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101,108`
+- `${isPending ? "loading" : ""}` on a `btn` replaces the whole button content with a full-size spinner (text vanishes, looks broken).
+- **Fix:** Remove `loading` from className; put `{isPending && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm mr-2" />}` inside the button.
+
+### 15. `pollingInterval` is the 30s default — UI feels frozen
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24` → `pollingInterval: 30000`
+- Base is an L2; 30s update lag reads as broken.
+- **Fix:** `pollingInterval: 3000` (or lower).
+
+### 16. Default Alchemy key + bare `http()` fallback → public-RPC rate limits
+- **Files:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:16,29,32-35` (default key `IZYEU2cWBgnFmgiTAgpWD`, empty `rpcOverrides`); `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx` (`rpcFallbacks = […, http()]`, and with the default key the bare public `http()` is placed *before* Alchemy).
+- On Base this routes traffic to the rate-limited public endpoint. For a live payments app this will throttle reads/writes.
+- **Fix:** Set `NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` (and confirm it's actually set on Vercel, `vercel env ls`), or add a `rpcOverrides[8453]` pointing at a dedicated Base RPC. Remove the bare `http()` fallback so it doesn't silently hit public RPCs.
+
+### 17. Event history scans from block 0 on Base mainnet
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:29-34` → `fromBlock: 0n`
+- Base is at block ~33.7M; scanning from 0 every load (with `watch: true`) is extremely slow and will hammer/ rate-limit the RPC. The contract's `deployedOnBlock` is `33712450`.
+- **Fix:** `fromBlock: 33712450n` (the deploy block).
+
+### 18. `--radius-field: 9999rem` — pill-shaped inputs/textarea
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36,63` (both theme blocks)
+- The amount/recipient inputs and the memo `<textarea>` (`page.tsx:92`) render as pills and can clip content.
+- **Fix:** `--radius-field: 0.5rem;` in both `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks.
+
+### 19. Phantom wallet missing from the RainbowKit list
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx` (wallets array)
+- Many users have Phantom; it's not in the list, so they can't connect.
+- **Fix:** Add `phantomWallet` to the `wallets` array.
+
+### 20. No mobile deep-linking on transaction buttons
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (handlers `36-62`)
+- RainbowKit/WalletConnect v2 doesn't auto-deep-link. On mobile, tapping Approve/Send won't reliably open the wallet app to sign.
+- **Fix:** Add a `writeAndOpen` helper (fire the write first, then `setTimeout(openWallet, 2000)`), wrap **both** approve and pay calls, detect wallet from WC session data, and skip when `window.ethereum` exists (in-app browser).
+
+### 21. Amount input allows sending more than balance / no client-side guard
+- **File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:85-91`
+- Plain `type="number"` with no max/validation against `usdcBalance`; over-balance sends just revert onchain (and per #13, silently).
+- **Fix:** Consider `<IntegerInput>`/`<EtherInput>`-style handling or at least validate `amount <= balance` and disable Send otherwise.
+
